p.src:
This expands the energy-budget model from a workday to a life structure. In the earlier notation, an operator protects daily energy by filtering interactions: $E_{\mathrm{remain}}
=
E_0-\sum_i c_i.$ Lecture 122 asks us to widen the accounting: $C_{\mathrm{life}}
=
c_{\text{work}}
+
c_{\text{family}}
+
c_{\text{health}}
+
r.$ If company formation, children, and marriage all demand more at once, then reserve is the first buffer to shrink: $c_{\text{work}}\uparrow,\qquad
c_{\text{family}}\uparrow,\qquad
r\downarrow.$ The failure condition is not a moral judgment. It is a load condition: $c_{\text{work}}+c_{\text{family}}+c_{\text{health}}>C_{\mathrm{life}}.$

